    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "There's 12 titles and so whatever is involved with regards to agriculture from the farm to the fork if you will it is addressed in the bill and that's why it's so important all phases of agriculture are affected and we try to be of help in that regard as you know As every producer all around the country knows, farmers, ranchers, growers up and down Main Street, we're in a rough patch. And we've been that way for about four years in terms of prices going on the fifth year. Farm income down 52%, trade retaliation, mitigation payments, all the things that we don't need. So we knew from the first in Manhattan, Kansas when we first started out at Kansas State. We had to sit on the wagon tongue and, you know, listen to farmers. Senator Stabenot and I get along very well. She is a very effective and important partner in all of this. And so we got a bipartisan bicameral bill by working together. And we knew that farmers needed above everything else, certainty and predictability. There you got the whole speech.",
