        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "Counting votes is necessary to pass legislation.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "The nutrition title was one of the titles members felt strongly about.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "It is reasonable to respect members' strong feelings about particular titles in the Farm Bill.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Failing to pass a farm bill due to insistence on a single issue undermines the broader benefits of the farm bill.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Compromise is not inherently negative in Washington policymaking.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Most people expect lawmakers to cooperate and produce results.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "The farm bill was passed after two years of effort.",
        "confidence": 0.9
