    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72741.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "Well, that would be what I call a mitigation payment. I guess you can call anything you want to. Farmers said at the beginning, and we also chimed in. The farmers don't want aid. They want trade. So progress in China, which I think is occurring, and China buying, not to the extent that they used to, but they need to step up. That helps our relationship with China. They become more dependent on us. It's a national security issue as well. That's all across the board. So if the administration focuses on restoring our trade relationships and recapturing our markets, there won't be any need for that. I mean, farmers are used to working with the market and the cycles that we experience. What they are not used to is the government intervening with tariff and then having a tariff retaliation. We'll be holding hearings on that in the coming year.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
